When that venerable Brahmin's wife was about to give birth to a child, she became very worried.
Being very anxious, she went to Arjuna and pleaded with him, "Please save my child from death,
save it.""

Sa upasprushya shuchyambho namaskritya maheshwaram.
Remembering the divine weapons, he produces the Gandiva. 36. Meaning of the word

Saha - He (Arjuna); Upasprashya - by touching; Shuchi - pure; Ambha - water; Namah - salutations; Maha - to Shiva; Ishwaram -
To Shiva; Divyan - divine; Astrani - one's projections; Samsmritya - by remembering; Sajyam - the bow's string;
Gandivam - one's bow on the Gandiva; Adade - fixed. By touching pure water, by bowing to Lord Maheshwar, and by chanting mantras for his divine weapons,
Arjun mounted the string of his bow, Gandiva. Meaning: The teachers have indicated that since the Brahmin had disrespected Lord Krishna,
therefore Arjun very cleverly greeted Shivji, who had taught him the method of using the mantras of Pashupatastra. Nyarunatsutikagaram sharairnanastrayojitah.
Tiryaguṛdhāmaṃ, Pārthaḥ, Śarāpāṇḍraṃ. 37. Meaning of the word

